WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.823
Two ablations are central.

00:00:01.903 --> 00:00:08.264
Sweeping the split-hardness parameter alpha shows
harder splits give better dataset-wise

00:00:08.344 --> 00:00:10.679
win rates against the MLP kernel,

00:00:10.759 --> 00:00:18.218
climbing from about fourteen percent when splits
are soft to nearly thirty-five percent at the hardest,

00:00:18.298 --> 00:00:21.511
all above the radial basis function baseline.

00:00:21.591 --> 00:00:25.317
Sweeping tree depth reproduces the degeneracy story.

00:00:25.397 --> 00:00:30.733
The authors also verify empirically that oblivious
trees, as used by NODE,

00:00:30.813 --> 00:00:34.100
induce the same kernel as ordinary soft trees.
